# Stack rules (Nuxt 4 / Vue)

- **TypeScript:** `strict` and `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`. No `any` without a written justification on the call site.
- **Locale:** British English in UI copy (`colour`, not `color` in user-facing text). Code identifiers may use `backgroundColour`.
- **Persistence:** browser `localStorage` only. Soft-deleted tasks retained 30 days. Never invent a backend.
- **Icons:** Font Awesome Pro via deep imports in `app/plugins/fontawesome.ts`. Never import whole style packs. Token via `FONTAWESOME_PACKAGE_TOKEN` only.
- **Markdown:** sanitise HTML from Markdown descriptions before render (XSS even for local data).
- **Ownership:** backend = `app/composables/**`, `app/utils/**`, `app/types/**`. Frontend = components, pages, layouts, assets, plugins, `app.vue`, `app.config.ts`, `public/**`. Shared manifests stay orchestrator-owned.
- **Deploy:** `nuxt generate` with Nitro `github_pages` preset; custom domain `tasks.slydave.com`.
- **Tooling:** Prettier + ESLint (warnings as errors) + `nuxt typecheck` + Vitest + `npm audit --audit-level=high`.
